   "roundness": null
  },
  {
   "id": "cl",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 838,
   "width": 689,
   "height": 21,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100033,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700231,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "The send path - and the biggest single optimization in the design",
   "originalText": "The send path - and the biggest single optimization in the design",
   "fontSize": 17,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "snd",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 876,
   "width": 860,
   "height": 200,
   "strokeColor": "#1e293b",
   "backgroundColor": "#1e293b",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100034,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700238,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "snd_t",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "snd_t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 38,
   "y": 908,
   "width": 844,
   "height": 135,
   "strokeColor": "#ffffff",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100035,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700245,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "client  ->  LB  ->  web server\n  1. authenticate; rate-limit (a compromised account is a spam cannon)\n  2. validate: size limit, recipient count, header sanity\n  3. store the body ONCE, content-addressed; attachments by content hash\n  4. write the sender's own copy into their Sent folder\n  5. SHORT-CIRCUIT: for recipients on OUR OWN domain, write their\n     metadata rows directly - no SMTP, no network, no external delivery\n  6. for external recipients: enqueue onto the outbound queue\n  ->  202 Accepted",
   "originalText": "client  ->  LB  ->  web server\n  1. authenticate; rate-limit (a compromised account is a spam cannon)\n  2. validate: size limit, recipient count, header sanity\n  3. store the body ONCE, content-addressed; attachments by content hash\n  4. write the sender's own copy into their Sent folder\n  5. SHORT-CIRCUIT: for recipients on OUR OWN domain, write their\n     metadata rows directly - no SMTP, no network, no external delivery\n  6. for external recipients: enqueue onto the outbound queue\n  ->  202 Accepted",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "snd",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "out",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1096,
   "width": 860,
   "height": 130,
   "strokeColor": "#1e293b",
   "backgroundColor": "#1e293b",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100036,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700252,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "out_t",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "out_t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 38,
   "y": 1108,
   "width": 844,
   "height": 105,
   "strokeColor": "#ffffff",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100037,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700259,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "outbound SMTP worker\n  7. DNS: look up the MX records for the recipient's domain\n  8. choose a sending IP by reputation and mail class\n  9. connect, STARTTLS, DKIM-sign, transfer\n       2xx -> delivered\n       4xx -> TEMPORARY: requeue with backoff, retry for up to ~3 days\n       5xx -> PERMANENT: generate a bounce back to the sender",
   "originalText": "outbound SMTP worker\n  7. DNS: look up the MX records for the recipient's domain\n  8. choose a sending IP by reputation and mail class\n  9. connect, STARTTLS, DKIM-sign, transfer\n       2xx -> delivered\n       4xx -> TEMPORARY: requeue with backoff, retry for up to ~3 days\n       5xx -> PERMANENT: generate a bounce back to the sender",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "out",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "cn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 940,
   "y": 876,
   "width": 591,
   "height": 75,
   "strokeColor": "#047857",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100038,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700266,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Step 5 is easy to miss and it is the biggest single optimization here. A large\nprovider's internal mail - one user to another on the same domain - never\ntouches SMTP at all. It is a metadata row insert: orders of magnitude cheaper\nthan the external path, and it sidesteps the entire deliverability problem. For\na provider with a billion users, a large fraction of all mail is internal.",
   "originalText": "Step 5 is easy to miss and it is the biggest single optimization here. A large\nprovider's internal mail - one user to another on the same domain - never\ntouches SMTP at all. It is a metadata row insert: orders of magnitude cheaper\nthan the external path, and it sidesteps the entire deliverability problem. For\na provider with a billion users, a large fraction of all mail is internal.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "cn2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 940,
   "y": 976,
   "width": 599,
   "height": 90,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100039,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700273,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Steps 7-9 are why outbound is a WORKER and not a request handler. A destination\nserver can be down for hours, and SMTP's contract is that a 4xx means 'try again\nlater' - for up to several days by convention. So the outbound queue holds\nmessages with a retry schedule spanning DAYS, and there is no request waiting on\nany of it. That is a fundamentally different service shape from anything else in\nthe design.",
   "originalText": "Steps 7-9 are why outbound is a WORKER and not a request handler. A destination\nserver can be down for hours, and SMTP's contract is that a 4xx means 'try again\nlater' - for up to several days by convention. So the outbound queue holds\nmessages with a retry schedule spanning DAYS, and there is no request waiting on\nany of it. That is a fundamentally different service shape from anything else in\nthe design.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "cn3",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 940,
   "y": 1096,
   "width": 599,
   "height": 60,
   "strokeColor": "#b45309",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100040,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700280,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "It is also why outbound capacity CANNOT AUTOSCALE: new sending IPs need weeks of\nwarm-up, so outbound send capacity is a weeks-ahead provisioning decision rather\nthan an autoscaling one. An odd constraint in an otherwise elastic system, and\nit catches people out.",
   "originalText": "It is also why outbound capacity CANNOT AUTOSCALE: new sending IPs need weeks of\nwarm-up, so outbound send capacity is a weeks-ahead provisioning decision rather\nthan an autoscaling one. An odd constraint in an otherwise elastic system, and\nit catches people out.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "cn4",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 940,
   "y": 1180,
   "width": 569,
   "height": 75,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100041,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700287,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "The read path, for completeness: Redis for recent messages (mail access is\nheavily recency-skewed), then headers only from the metadata store, then the\nbody by content hash for the OPENED message alone - and attachments served\ndirectly from object storage by pre-signed URL, so a 25 MB download never\npasses through the API tier.",
   "originalText": "The read path, for completeness: Redis for recent messages (mail access is\nheavily recency-skewed), then headers only from the metadata store, then the\nbody by content hash for the OPENED message alone - and attachments served\ndirectly from object storage by pre-signed URL, so a 25 MB download never\npasses through the API tier.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "d4",
   "type": "line",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1268,
   "width": 1680,
   "height": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#cbd5e1",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100042,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700294,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "points": [
