  {
   "id": "dl",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1286,
   "width": 689,
   "height": 21,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100043,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700301,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Six services, and each boundary is forced by a genuine difference",
   "originalText": "Six services, and each boundary is forced by a genuine difference",
   "fontSize": 17,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "dn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1324,
   "width": 963,
   "height": 211,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100044,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700308,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "SMTP inbound servers      they speak a protocol from 1982 to STRANGERS - hostile, unauthenticated traffic - and their\n                          scaling driver is inbound connection count. Isolating them contains the blast radius of a\n                          protocol-level exploit.\nSMTP outbound workers     the opposite shape: LONG-LIVED RETRYING connections to third parties over hours or days, with\n                          throughput gated by other people's servers. They also carry the IP reputation, so which IP a\n                          message leaves from is a routing decision that belongs here and nowhere else.\nweb / API servers         stateless HTTPS; the primary client interface\nreal-time servers         they hold STATEFUL WebSocket connections, so they need draining on deploy - and mixing that\n                          into a stateless HTTP tier would impose connection-draining semantics on every release\nthe search service        a completely different engine with an inverted index, whose workload (write-heavy,\n                          read-light) is the inverse of everything else here\nmail processing workers    the asynchronous work - spam, virus, fan-out, indexing - that must NOT sit between an\n                          inbound connection and its acknowledgement",
   "originalText": "SMTP inbound servers      they speak a protocol from 1982 to STRANGERS - hostile, unauthenticated traffic - and their\n                          scaling driver is inbound connection count. Isolating them contains the blast radius of a\n                          protocol-level exploit.\nSMTP outbound workers     the opposite shape: LONG-LIVED RETRYING connections to third parties over hours or days, with\n                          throughput gated by other people's servers. They also carry the IP reputation, so which IP a\n                          message leaves from is a routing decision that belongs here and nowhere else.\nweb / API servers         stateless HTTPS; the primary client interface\nreal-time servers         they hold STATEFUL WebSocket connections, so they need draining on deploy - and mixing that\n                          into a stateless HTTP tier would impose connection-draining semantics on every release\nthe search service        a completely different engine with an inverted index, whose workload (write-heavy,\n                          read-light) is the inverse of everything else here\nmail processing workers    the asynchronous work - spam, virus, fan-out, indexing - that must NOT sit between an\n                          inbound connection and its acknowledgement",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "dn2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1580,
   "width": 979,
   "height": 16,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100045,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700315,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "No component's scaling driver is shared with another's, which is the practical payoff of drawing the boundaries this way.",
   "originalText": "No component's scaling driver is shared with another's, which is the practical payoff of drawing the boundaries this way.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "d5",
   "type": "line",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1620,
   "width": 1680,
   "height": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#cbd5e1",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100046,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700322,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "points": [
