   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "421 Service not available   /   4xx   ->   'retry later'\nand well-behaved senders WILL. So under overload the system pushes\nlegitimate mail back onto the SENDER's queue rather than dropping it.",
   "originalText": "421 Service not available   /   4xx   ->   'retry later'\nand well-behaved senders WILL. So under overload the system pushes\nlegitimate mail back onto the SENDER's queue rather than dropping it.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "bp",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "en",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 900,
   "y": 1676,
   "width": 584,
   "height": 60,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100050,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700350,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "The number that actually varies is not the diurnal curve: it is SPAM VOLUME,\nwhich is adversarial rather than periodic. A campaign can multiply the inbound\nconnection rate with no warning, so the inbound tier is sized FOR ATTACK, not\nfor legitimate mail.",
   "originalText": "The number that actually varies is not the diurnal curve: it is SPAM VOLUME,\nwhich is adversarial rather than periodic. A campaign can multiply the inbound\nconnection rate with no warning, so the inbound tier is sized FOR ATTACK, not\nfor legitimate mail.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "sh",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1786,
   "width": 342,
   "height": 17,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100051,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700357,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "What gets shed under overload, in order",
   "originalText": "What gets shed under overload, in order",
   "fontSize": 14,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "shn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1814,
   "width": 971,
   "height": 130,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100052,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700364,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "1  search index writes                deferred into a backlog. Search goes stale; nothing else is affected, and because\n                                      search is read-light, nobody notices quickly.\n2  inbound from LOW-REPUTATION IPs    get 4xx first. Reputation-weighted admission means legitimate senders are the last\n                                      to be throttled.\n3  non-urgent outbound                bulk and marketing classes are delayed behind transactional mail - the same class\n                                      separation that reputation management needs anyway.\n4  NEVER shed anything already 250-OK'd      that is an ownership promise.\n5  NEVER shed inbound from high-reputation senders    making Gmail retry is a reputation risk in both directions.",
   "originalText": "1  search index writes                deferred into a backlog. Search goes stale; nothing else is affected, and because\n                                      search is read-light, nobody notices quickly.\n2  inbound from LOW-REPUTATION IPs    get 4xx first. Reputation-weighted admission means legitimate senders are the last\n                                      to be throttled.\n3  non-urgent outbound                bulk and marketing classes are delayed behind transactional mail - the same class\n                                      separation that reputation management needs anyway.\n4  NEVER shed anything already 250-OK'd      that is an ownership promise.\n5  NEVER shed inbound from high-reputation senders    making Gmail retry is a reputation risk in both directions.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
