  {
   "id": "gl",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 2228,
   "width": 646,
   "height": 21,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100063,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700441,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "One inbound message can be five orders of magnitude of writes",
   "originalText": "One inbound message can be five orders of magnitude of writes",
   "fontSize": 17,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "ml",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 2266,
   "width": 900,
   "height": 74,
   "strokeColor": "#1e293b",
   "backgroundColor": "#1e293b",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100064,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700448,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "ml_t",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "ml_t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 38,
   "y": 2280,
   "width": 884,
   "height": 45,
   "strokeColor": "#ffffff",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100065,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700455,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "one email to a 50,000-member list\n   =  50,000 metadata inserts  +  50,000 index writes\n      +  50,000 push notifications        - arriving as ONE SMTP transaction",
   "originalText": "one email to a 50,000-member list\n   =  50,000 metadata inserts  +  50,000 index writes\n      +  50,000 push notifications        - arriving as ONE SMTP transaction",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "ml",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "gn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 960,
   "y": 2266,
   "width": 591,
   "height": 60,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100066,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700462,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Mitigations: fan out asynchronously in batches rather than synchronously (which\nthe queue already provides), cap recipients per message, and - the reason\ncontent-addressing matters again - store the body ONCE, so 50,000 copies cost\n50,000 small rows rather than 2.5 GB.",
   "originalText": "Mitigations: fan out asynchronously in batches rather than synchronously (which\nthe queue already provides), cap recipients per message, and - the reason\ncontent-addressing matters again - store the body ONCE, so 50,000 copies cost\n50,000 small rows rather than 2.5 GB.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "gn2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 2374,
   "width": 1011,
   "height": 113,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100067,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700469,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Degradation, and note how much SMTP gives for free: the search cluster failing costs only search; real-time servers failing\nmeans clients fall back to polling; the cache failing is slower but correct; outbound workers failing means messages\naccumulate in a durable queue with nothing lost; and INBOUND SMTP FAILING MEANS SENDERS RETRY FOR DAYS - so a multi-hour\ninbound outage delays mail rather than losing it, which is the single most valuable reliability property the protocol gives\nyou. Only one failure is deliberately hard: a metadata partition losing quorum makes that partition's users unable to read or\nreceive, chosen over risking loss. And a non-empty dead-letter queue is an INCIDENT, not a debugging aid, because every\nmessage in it was already acknowledged with 250 OK.",
   "originalText": "Degradation, and note how much SMTP gives for free: the search cluster failing costs only search; real-time servers failing\nmeans clients fall back to polling; the cache failing is slower but correct; outbound workers failing means messages\naccumulate in a durable queue with nothing lost; and INBOUND SMTP FAILING MEANS SENDERS RETRY FOR DAYS - so a multi-hour\ninbound outage delays mail rather than losing it, which is the single most valuable reliability property the protocol gives\nyou. Only one failure is deliberately hard: a metadata partition losing quorum makes that partition's users unable to read or\nreceive, chosen over risking loss. And a non-empty dead-letter queue is an INCIDENT, not a debugging aid, because every\nmessage in it was already acknowledged with 250 OK.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "gn3",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 2532,
   "width": 987,
   "height": 113,
   "strokeColor": "#b45309",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100068,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700476,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "The structural gap worth naming: NO END-TO-END ENCRYPTION. Server-side spam filtering, virus scanning, search indexing and\nthreading all require reading message content - so E2EE is fundamentally incompatible with most of this design's features,\nnot merely unbuilt. Alongside it: shared mailboxes do not fit partitioning by user_id (support@company.com read by twelve\npeople is genuinely shared, and the pseudo-user workaround breaks per-user read state, which is what a shared inbox needs\nmost); Message-Id deduplication has no defined window (too short duplicates a slow retry, too long grows unboundedly, and\nthe right value depends on every sending provider's conventions); and unread counters drift, with a recompute that scans a\nuser's mail - expensive for a million-message mailbox, at a frequency nobody has priced.",
   "originalText": "The structural gap worth naming: NO END-TO-END ENCRYPTION. Server-side spam filtering, virus scanning, search indexing and\nthreading all require reading message content - so E2EE is fundamentally incompatible with most of this design's features,\nnot merely unbuilt. Alongside it: shared mailboxes do not fit partitioning by user_id (support@company.com read by twelve\npeople is genuinely shared, and the pseudo-user workaround breaks per-user read state, which is what a shared inbox needs\nmost); Message-Id deduplication has no defined window (too short duplicates a slow retry, too long grows unboundedly, and\nthe right value depends on every sending provider's conventions); and unread counters drift, with a recompute that scans a\nuser's mail - expensive for a million-message mailbox, at a frequency nobody has priced.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  }
 ],
